Task #952: Alert ops when merge-conflict recovery storms a single file

Adds threshold-based spike detection to the operator dashboard at
/admin/merge-conflict-recovery so a single file path crossing N
conflicts within a rolling window pages on-call instead of waiting
for someone to refresh the page.

Changes:
- src/repositories/merge-conflict-recovery.repository.ts
  Adds pure projection `summarizeFileBurstsWithinWindow(events,
  windowMs, now?)` returning per-file counts + lastAt within the
  window. Sorted desc by count.

- src/pages/admin/AdminMergeConflictRecoveryPage.tsx
  - Configurable threshold (count + window minutes) with sensible
    defaults (5 conflicts / 60 min) persisted to localStorage.
    Bounded inputs: count >= 2, window 5..1440 minutes.
  - New "Spike detection" card showing the threshold inputs, a top-
    of-window proximity bar (current top-file count vs threshold),
    and per-file proximity bars for the 10 worst files in the
    window. Card border / icon turn destructive when any file is
    over the line.
  - `useFileBurstAlerts` hook fires `createAdminAlert` with
    alertType `merge_conflict_recovery_storm`, severity `high`,
    contextType `merge_conflict_recovery`, contextId = file path,
    and metadata (count, threshold, window, last_event_at). Dedup
    keyed on (file, threshold) with a 1h cool-down stored in
    localStorage; in-flight set prevents double-fire from the
    refetch interval. Errors are swallowed (logged) so a flaky
    insert doesn't break the dashboard.

Alerts flow into the existing alert center (admin_alerts /
AdminAlertCenterPage) — no new pipeline added.

Verification: tsc --noEmit and eslint both clean on touched files.

Follow-ups proposed (#974 server-side firing, #975 team-wide
threshold storage, #976 tests for spike detection).
